# Mutable array invariance

Verifies an integer array cannot initialize an array whose mutable element
contract also admits strings.

>>> source
let integers: int[] = [1, 2]
let values: (int | string)[] = integers

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: type mismatch: binding `values` expects `(int64 | string)[]`, expression produces `int64[]` at Span { start: 60, end: 68 }

<<< exit
1
